<title>NORWAY: Statoil's Heidrun oilfield returns from turnaround.</title>
<headline>Statoil's Heidrun oilfield returns from turnaround.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Friday it had restarted oil production at the Heidrun field following a scheduled maintenance shutdown.</p>
<p>Heidrun was shut for turnaround on September 2.</p>
<p>&quot;Production at Heidrun began this morning,&quot; a Statoil spokesman said.</p>
<p>In August the field produced an average 232,440 barrels per day (bpd), slightly off plateau output of 250,000 bpd.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
